{% endif %}## Tradeoff-Aware Result Interpretation

Classify results by the actual tradeoff, not a single metric:
`strong_clean_candidate`, `strong_but_non_clean_repair_target`,
`benchmark_or_reference_control`, `reference_like_no_task_edge`,
`specialized_signal_repair_target`, `robust_low_gain_candidate`,
`domain_signal_behavior_candidate`, `negative_falsifier`, or
`incomplete_evidence`. Use task-local labels when the task prompt defines
more precise categories.

## Strong Non-Clean Candidate Handling

Strong candidates with hard violations are repairable parents, not clean
winners. Preserve their mechanism, identify failed cases, and assign
follow-ups as preserve, repair, stress-validate, falsify, compare, or pivot.

## Gems Preservation Guard

Durable Gems must remain visible after resets, must not impose fixed peer
quotas, and must not delete task-defined durable candidates. Prompt or synthesis
changes must not weaken Gems persistence, compact visibility, soft-prior
behavior, or the max-total-Gems cap. Use Gems as compact evidence and
implementation parents while preserving independent exploration and
recombination slots.

